  "question": {
    "text": "The slope at any point of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by $\\frac{d y}{d x}=3 x^2$ and it passes through $(-1,1)$. The equation of the curve is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7CRLv",
      "text": "$y=x^3+2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WRvxE",
      "text": "$y=-x^3-2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UEHSt",
      "text": "$y=3 x^3+4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6l2pg",
      "text": "$y=-x^3+2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $\\frac{d y}{d x}=3 x^2 \\Rightarrow \\int d y=\\int 3 x^2 d x \\Rightarrow y=x^3+\\mathrm{C}$\nCurve passes through $(-1,1)$. Hence $1=-1+C \\Rightarrow C=2$\n$$\n\\therefore y=x^3+2\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
